<title>USA: Manufactured Home enters interest rate swap.</title>
<headline>Manufactured Home enters interest rate swap.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Manufactured Home Communities Inc said Wednesday it entered into a 14-month interest rate swap agreement for $100 million of floating rate mortgage notes due 1998.</p>
<p>It said the swap efectively fixes the company's interest expense for that period at a rate of 6.6 percent.</p>
<p>As a result of the swap, Manufactrured Home has effectively fixed its interest rates on $200 million of mortgage debt through 2001 and beyond.</p>
<p>The company, which owns and operates mobile homes, is a self-administered equity real estate investment trust.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
